    Default RAW decoder
prefs-default-decoder-description
    What the inspector's RAW decoder starts with, and what batches use. Automatic is Adobe DNG Converter when it is installed, else LibRaw. The two crop and demosaic differently, so their frames of the same shot don't line up.
prefs-decoder-automatic
    Automatic
prefs-camera-profile
    Camera profile
prefs-profile-adobe-standard
    Adobe Standard
prefs-profile-camera-standard
    Camera Standard
prefs-profile-none
    None (the colors in the file)
prefs-camera-profile-description
    The installed Adobe profile that colors LibRaw-decoded RAW files. DNGs and Adobe-converted frames carry their own. Recorded with each render.
prefs-profile-folders
    Camera profile folders
prefs-profile-folders-description
    Searched for .dcp files before Adobe's folders. A profile is used when its file name starts with the camera's make and model, for example "Canon EOS R5 Adobe Standard.dcp".
prefs-applies-when-run-ends
    Stacking is under way: a change here applies once it ends.
prefs-no-profile-folders
    No folders added.
prefs-remove-profile-folder
    Remove
prefs-add-profile-folder
    Add Folder…
prefs-adobe-profile-folders
    Adobe profile folders found
prefs-no-adobe-profile-folders
    None found. Adobe's free DNG Converter installs these profiles.
prefs-converter
    Converter
prefs-converter-description
    Used by the Adobe DNG Converter RAW decoder. Choose the application if it isn't in its default location.
prefs-converter-unavailable
    Not available on this platform
prefs-converter-found
    Found
prefs-converter-not-found
    Not found. It is free from Adobe; restart Deptheos after installing it.
prefs-converter-get
    Get It
prefs-converter-jobs
    Parallel conversions
prefs-converter-jobs-description
    How many RAW files are converted at once. More is faster until the CPU or disk is saturated; each conversion also uses some memory.
prefs-converter-uncompressed
    Uncompressed conversions
prefs-converter-uncompressed-description
    Write the converted DNGs without compression. A stack of them runs about a quarter faster, but each takes twice the disk: about 270 MB for a 45 MP frame instead of 130 MB. The conversions are kept until the stack has read them for the last time, and Depth reads every frame twice, so a 200-frame Depth stack needs about 54 GB free instead of 26 GB.
prefs-graphics
    Graphics
prefs-gpu
    GPU
prefs-gpu-description
    The GPU that stacks, paints and prepares images. Software rendering runs on the CPU, as on a computer without a GPU: many times slower. Takes effect the next time Deptheos starts.
prefs-gpu-automatic
    Automatic (the fastest GPU)
prefs-gpu-software
    Software rendering (on the CPU, slow)
prefs-gpu-dedicated
    <name> (dedicated)
prefs-gpu-integrated
    <name> (integrated)
prefs-gpu-cpu
    <name> (software, on the CPU)
prefs-gpu-not-found
    <name> (not found)
prefs-gpu-in-use
    In use: <device>
prefs-gpu-none-started
    No GPU could be started.
prefs-gpu-restart
    Restart Deptheos to use it.
prefs-gpu-forced
    DEPTHEOS_SOFTWARE_GPU is set, which overrides this.
prefs-gpu-failed
    This choice couldn't start, so Deptheos is using the fastest GPU it found. <reason>
prefs-gpu-missing
    <name> wasn't found, so Deptheos is using the fastest GPU.
prefs-memory
    Memory
prefs-read-ahead
    Frame read-ahead (MB)
prefs-read-ahead-description
    Decoded JPEG, PNG and TIFF frames held in memory ahead of stacking. Lower it on a computer with little memory; above the default rarely helps.
prefs-diagnostics
    Diagnostics
prefs-verbose-logging
    Verbose logging
prefs-verbose-logging-description
    Until Deptheos quits. Adds detail to the log for bug reports (Help ▸ Save Diagnostics…).
update-available-title
    Update available
update-available
    Deptheos <version> is available. You have <current>.
update-download
    Download
update-up-to-date
    Deptheos <version> is the latest version.
update-failed-unreachable
    Deptheos couldn't check for updates. The release page couldn't be reached. Check the internet connection, then try again.
update-failed-refused
    Deptheos couldn't check for updates. The release page answered with an error. Try again later.
update-failed-unreadable
    Deptheos couldn't check for updates. The reply about the latest release couldn't be read.
update-failed-not-a-version
    Deptheos couldn't check for updates. The latest release is tagged "<tag>", which isn't a version number Deptheos recognizes.
