    Deptheos Diagnostics <date>
diagnostics-zip-archive
    Zip archive
diagnostics-saved
    Saved <name>. Email it to <address>: it holds the logs and crash reports, so don't attach it to a public issue.
diagnostics-save-failed
    The diagnostics couldn't be saved.
cli-tool-missing
    This copy of Deptheos has no command line tool.
cli-tool-not-installed
    Move Deptheos to the Applications folder and open it from there, then install the command line tool.
cli-tool-already-installed
    The deptheos command is installed in <folder>. Type "deptheos --help" in Terminal to start.
cli-tool-install-title
    Install the command line tool?
cli-tool-install-description
    This puts the deptheos command in <link>, linked to the one inside Deptheos, so it runs in Terminal and is updated with the app. macOS may ask for an administrator password.
cli-tool-install-description-replacing
    This puts the deptheos command in <link>, linked to the one inside Deptheos, so it runs in Terminal and is updated with the app. macOS may ask for an administrator password. It replaces the deptheos command there now (<old>).
cli-tool-outside-applications
    Deptheos isn't in the Applications folder. If you move or delete it, the deptheos command stops working.
cli-tool-taken
    There is already a deptheos command at <link>, and it isn't Deptheos's. Remove it, then install the command line tool again.
cli-tool-link-changed
    What is at <link> changed after you were asked, so nothing was replaced. Install the command line tool again to see what it would replace.
cli-tool-install
    Install
cli-tool-admin-prompt
    Deptheos wants to install the deptheos command.
cli-tool-installed
    The deptheos command is installed. Type "deptheos --help" in Terminal to start.
cli-tool-install-failed
    The command line tool couldn't be installed.
